{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0852a708a82e799d75b8b53357e3e9244057a3aeddb502cc1767c6c0e5d9db26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Changes move through six stages — intake, apply, review, hydrate, ship, review-PR — each producing a persistent artifact such as intake.md, plan.md, or a PR."},{"claim_ids":["clm_13d27fff53dadd589d4f5f4b8f4c86253ba2bdbd1eadde69e844e5477ea02bf7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A project constitution (fab/project/constitution.md) with MUST/SHOULD/MUST NOT rules is checked by every plan and review; it and config.yaml are the only required of five config files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1418936003b7402fbaea4fad7dc2ca76f7f9b53bc31b6be9293333782b6dddf4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each change is a self-contained folder under fab/changes/ holding intake.md, plan.md, and a .status.yaml state file symlinked at the repo root while active."},{"claim_ids":["clm_15a6ef3e94dce14f16c0524da32c09e1efb37d09c9f528d283ad64371e1815cf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Parallelism relies on git worktree isolation: wt create makes an isolated worktree, fab sync runs automatically in each new worktree, and self-contained change folders avoid shared state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1ad29eb2ba8434bb3b7728baef654fc2167c3519cfdd74145eddf19c6d85673e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: building Fab Kit from source requires Go for the binaries under src/go/ and the just task runner for build, test, and release recipes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65e4713477d443c6eda2aca577c9c893cee97f7c266e8b4518a6562e64323f18"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Review runs in a separate sub-agent context; /fab-ff and /fab-fff auto-loop between apply and review up to 3 cycles, fixing issues before escalating to the user."},{"claim_ids":["clm_78fda2114021aed6726dbbba196c7d2bcf602c814db2b44a1a29b54444c01bc2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The fab CLI exposes subcommands including sync, config show/explain/set, doctor, operator, and batch new/switch/archive for worktree tab management."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7ad5a63812c3c12754b006072eea62801b84b33b303d80a2ef13d994990f42d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Learnings from each change are saved into docs/memory/, a domain-organized knowledge base committed to git and shared across the team; /docs-hydrate-memory can bootstrap it from Notion, Linear, or local files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_80e5973d6b733cb47f7412fa13e7dfc7a10405c73bb893f3f9ef226847c1065c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills are slash commands typed into an AI agent's chat (/fab-* in Claude Code, $fab-* in Codex), not terminal commands; each command runs one pipeline stage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b73a8aefd5af57902af462ea84f8dec69c6cbc41d3db0cb129a664148c824656"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The kit includes the fab CLI router (init/upgrade-repo/sync), companion tools wt for worktrees and idea for backlogs, and batch orchestration for parallel AI agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c7177dac9c6b1022068cdd189f2dacd30ed120c96ac5b637d48463618506bb11"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The optional /fab-operator skill is a long-running coordination layer in its own tmux pane that monitors and directs agents across panes, with auto-answering and dependency-aware spawning."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d8fe5c5d69d80af81c5d5b8b400e80ec12a62ace0a99e2a33112194ed53f5ee6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prompts are plain markdown with no SDK and no vendor lock-in, and the kit works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and Windsurf."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed93e5eaa55d0cd8b4a97a78c1ac155cd7c5247dcc9d9ebdb6bf22ffe91f2bd3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"SRAD is a four-dimension framework (signal strength, reversibility, agent competence, disambiguation type) whose grades aggregate into a confidence score gating /fab-ff and blocking when ambiguity is too high."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f2b384b9e7dc8f1cdbb92b094e188b92fcfd5c4b302c0b91778e298fb8c6b7fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Runtime dependencies include yq (YAML for status files), jq (JSON for settings merge during sync), gh (releases and PR workflows), and direnv (workspace env vars), installable via brew."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0852a708a82e799d75b8b53357e3e9244057a3aeddb502cc1767c6c0e5d9db26","clm_13d27fff53dadd589d4f5f4b8f4c86253ba2bdbd1eadde69e844e5477ea02bf7","clm_1418936003b7402fbaea4fad7dc2ca76f7f9b53bc31b6be9293333782b6dddf4","clm_15a6ef3e94dce14f16c0524da32c09e1efb37d09c9f528d283ad64371e1815cf","clm_1ad29eb2ba8434bb3b7728baef654fc2167c3519cfdd74145eddf19c6d85673e","clm_65e4713477d443c6eda2aca577c9c893cee97f7c266e8b4518a6562e64323f18","clm_78fda2114021aed6726dbbba196c7d2bcf602c814db2b44a1a29b54444c01bc2","clm_7ad5a63812c3c12754b006072eea62801b84b33b303d80a2ef13d994990f42d8","clm_80e5973d6b733cb47f7412fa13e7dfc7a10405c73bb893f3f9ef226847c1065c","clm_b73a8aefd5af57902af462ea84f8dec69c6cbc41d3db0cb129a664148c824656","clm_c7177dac9c6b1022068cdd189f2dacd30ed120c96ac5b637d48463618506bb11","clm_d8fe5c5d69d80af81c5d5b8b400e80ec12a62ace0a99e2a33112194ed53f5ee6","clm_ed93e5eaa55d0cd8b4a97a78c1ac155cd7c5247dcc9d9ebdb6bf22ffe91f2bd3","clm_f2b384b9e7dc8f1cdbb92b094e188b92fcfd5c4b302c0b91778e298fb8c6b7fd"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_57050ea2a58b46aa85440fe1fa30969f","id":"pg_f965c038dd105c72ab6a1ccbf552ce94","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sahil87-fab-kit-readme-md-7284adb0be5d-1ccbf552ce94.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6a7d8df1744a5715b664c5f8faf23e0e"],"title":"sahil87/fab-kit/README.md @ 7284adb0be5d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57050ea2a58b46aa85440fe1fa30969f"}
